WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:19.088
One day John Manly and I rode out to deliver a message for the squire.

2
00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:24.332
On our way home, we saw a teenage boy riding a stout black pony.

3
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:30.056
John and I watched as the boy rode the pony toward a gate near the road.

4
00:00:31.144 --> 00:00:33.225
On either side of the gate was a tall hedge.

5
00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:37.506
he crazy?"

6
00:00:37.786 --> 00:00:38.426
John murmured.

7
00:00:38.446 --> 00:00:41.807
"That gate is much too high for a pony that size to jump."

8
00:00:42.928 --> 00:00:44.868
The pony seemed to be thinking the same thing.

9
00:00:46.669 --> 00:00:49.510
When he reached the gate, he veered off to the right and stopped.

10
00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.371
"Hey!" the boy shouted.

11
00:00:54.331 --> 00:00:56.172
He spun the pony around and tried again.

12
00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.683
This time he thumped the pony's sides with his heels and gave him several cracks with his whip.

13
00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.427
But once again the pony refused the jump.

14
00:01:09.287 --> 00:01:10.869
Instead he darted off to the left.

15
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.031
"You rotten little thing!"

16
00:01:15.312 --> 00:01:16.152
the boy cried.

17
00:01:17.493 --> 00:01:19.394
He still didn't notice John and me watching.

18
00:01:21.336 --> 00:01:25.539
The boy wheeled the pony around and aimed him at the gate once again, kicking as hard as

19
00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:27.240
he could and lashing him with the whip.

20
00:01:29.056 --> 00:01:31.438
The pony's ears were flat back against his head.

21
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.862
This time the pony turned neither left nor right.

22
00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:40.826
He just stopped short, threw his head down, and bucked several times.

23
00:01:42.047 --> 00:01:43.288
The boy tried to hang on.

24
00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:45.530
But the last buck sent him flying.

25
00:01:47.311 --> 00:01:50.894
He went right over the pony's shoulder, landing headfirst in the thorny hedge.

26
00:01:52.736 --> 00:01:55.138
"Ow!" he yelled, thrashing around.

27
00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:57.600
"Stupid thorns!"

28
00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.284
Meanwhile the pony spun around and galloped off, his reins dangling.

29
00:02:07.147 --> 00:02:08.348
John burst out laughing.

30
00:02:08.788 --> 00:02:11.010
"That boy got what he deserved," he said.

31
00:02:12.291 --> 00:02:13.032
The boy heard him.

32
00:02:13.052 --> 00:02:15.554
"Help!" he called.

33
00:02:15.574 --> 00:02:21.219
"Come help me out of these thorns so I can catch that rotten pony and teach him a

34
00:02:21.299 --> 00:02:26.804
lesson!" "I think you're the one who needs the lesson, young man," John said.

35
00:02:27.884 --> 00:02:29.786
"And those thorns seem to be giving you one.

36
00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:34.909
Maybe next time you'll know better than to try to make your pony jump over such a high

37
00:02:34.969 --> 00:02:37.912
gate. Or to use the whip so cruelly."

38
00:02:40.273 --> 00:02:43.636
We rode off, with the boy's cries following us part of the way.

39
00:02:46.998 --> 00:02:49.921
When we reached the next intersection, John turned off to the right.

40
00:02:49.941 --> 00:02:54.164
"I think we'd better stop by Farmer Bushby's house, Beauty," he said.

41
00:02:55.212 --> 00:02:58.295
"That young man might be a liar as well as a bad rider.

42
00:02:59.336 --> 00:03:02.838
It might be better for that pony if we're there to tell his side of the story."

43
00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:07.542
We rode up to a farmhouse.

44
00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:12.286
A man was standing in the road looking back and forth with a worried expression.

45
00:03:13.407 --> 00:03:16.069
His wife was nearby, and she looked frightened too.

46
00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.032
The black pony was grazing in the yard.

47
00:03:20.053 --> 00:03:23.996
He was still wearing his saddle, but he looked much more content without his rider.

48
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.241
"Hello, Mr.

49
00:03:26.301 --> 00:03:28.422
Manly," the farmer said when he saw us.

50
00:03:30.103 --> 00:03:31.724
"Have you seen my boy anywhere?

51
00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.265
His pony just came home without him."

52
00:03:34.285 --> 00:03:38.347
"As a matter of fact, I have," John replied.

53
00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:43.030
"And after seeing the way he rides, his pony is better off without him."

54
00:03:44.371 --> 00:03:45.251
"What do you mean?"

55
00:03:45.752 --> 00:03:46.632
the farmer asked.

56
00:03:46.652 --> 00:03:53.436
"Well, sir, I saw your son whipping and kicking that good-looking pony to make him jump," John said.

57
00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.402
"But the pony knew better than to try to make it over a gate that was far too

58
00:03:58.442 --> 00:03:58.962
high for him.

59
00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:03.805
He finally kicked up his heels and tipped the young man into a thorn hedge.

60
00:04:04.926 --> 00:04:06.486
Your son wanted me to help him out.

61
00:04:07.787 --> 00:04:11.809
But I could tell that the boy had no injuries aside from the scratches the thorns were giving

62
00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:14.291
him, and so I decided to leave him where he was.

63
00:04:15.471 --> 00:04:18.733
I love horses, and it bothers me to see them treated badly."

64
00:04:19.754 --> 00:04:21.515
The farmer's wife was crying by now.

65
00:04:21.535 --> 00:04:23.936
"Oh, poor Bill!"

66
00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:25.021
she sobbed.

67
00:04:25.941 --> 00:04:28.023
"We should go find him and help him."

68
00:04:28.043 --> 00:04:33.486
"I think I'd better go by myself, my dear," the farmer said with a sigh.

69
00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:38.470
"This is not the first time Bill has mistreated that pony, or the second either.

70
00:04:39.751 --> 00:04:42.072
It's time to put a stop to it and teach him a lesson."

71
00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:44.994
He nodded toward John.

72
00:04:45.014 --> 00:04:48.237
"Thank you for letting us know about this, Mr.

73
00:04:48.277 --> 00:04:51.359
Manly." "You're welcome," John said.

74
00:04:51.379 --> 00:04:52.740
"Good luck with your boy."

75
00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.342
When we got home, James was there to remove my saddle and groom me.

76
00:04:59.522 --> 00:05:01.944
While they worked, John told him what had happened.

77
00:05:02.964 --> 00:05:04.665
Soon the two of them were both chuckling.

78
00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:08.487
"I know the boy you mean," James said.

79
00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:12.209
"And you were right about his needing that lesson.

80
00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.971
He's always been careless about animals.

81
00:05:16.371 --> 00:05:18.413
Maybe this will teach him to treat them better."

82
00:05:19.493 --> 00:05:21.134
"I hope so," John replied.

83
00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:24.556
"Only a coward is cruel to helpless animals.

84
00:05:25.705 --> 00:05:27.529
At least this coward is still only a boy.

85
00:05:28.611 --> 00:05:31.879
If his father can get him to change his ways, there may be hope for him yet."
